Caddy is a TypeScript port of the algebraic modeling API of build123d
(https://github.com/gumyr/build123d), whose NOTICE reads:

    build123d
    Copyright (c) 2022–2025 The build123d Contributors

    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the "License");
    you may not use this file except in compliance with the License.
    You may obtain a copy of the License at:

        http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

    This project was originally derived from portions of the CadQuery codebase
    (https://github.com/CadQuery/cadquery) but has since been extensively
    refactored and restructured into an independent system.
    CadQuery is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Statement of changes: Caddy re-implements build123d 0.13.0's algebraic API in TypeScript. Python
modules were rewritten as TypeScript classes and functions with JavaScript naming (camelCase),
Python operators were replaced by named methods, the builder/context-manager API was omitted, and
the OCP (Python) kernel bindings were replaced by the native @roonieone/occt-native package.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Caddy's material catalog is a TypeScript port of bd_materials
(https://github.com/bernhard-42/bd_materials), Copyright 2026 Bernhard Walter, licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0.

Statement of changes: src/materials ports bd_materials 0.2.5 to TypeScript. The Python modules were
rewritten with JavaScript naming (camelCase) and trailing options objects, frozen dataclasses
became interfaces and immutable catalog objects, and the material, finish and process registries
were restructured for the npm package layout; it is not the original bd_materials.

